      "comment": "Goblin's Dread, the goblin lair inside the Windspire: an instanced dungeon. Each party plays its own copy (crates/server/src/directory/mod.rs); a copy lives on for 30 minutes after the last player leaves it. Its portal stands on a ledge hidden behind the Windspire's waterfall (its door in content/regions/emberholm/doors.json). Inside is a space of its own: everything is placed round its own origin, over nothing, and its boxes and decks are all that's solid there (src/engine/world/dungeons.ts, crates/engine/src/open/dungeon.rs). Boxes are solid below their top (floors and walls); decks are floors you can walk under. `arrive` is where you come in, `exit` the portal back out (F within r), `fall`: below it you are back at `arrive`. Heights (top) are above its origin. Map convention as Emberholm's: north is +Z, east is -X; facing 0 looks north. What it looks like inside is its dressing (docs/world.md, Dressing a Cave): the hall and tunnel its walls bound, the back of the falls, its torches, props, nets, loot and pictures, and the light the cave's colours are baked from.",
